craftflow-plugin

Concepts (not code) in the following modules are ported from grok-build:

  https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build
  Copyright (c) xAI
  Apache License 2.0

- `plugins/craftflow/scripts/craftflow_safe_shell_guard.py` — ported from
  `xai-grok-hooks`'s example guard pack (`safe-shell-guard.sh` +
  `no-recursive-grep-guard.py`): an absolute denylist of catastrophic shell
  command patterns (`rm -rf /`, `mkfs`, fork bombs) plus an opt-in
  recursive-grep-against-a-broad-path advisory check.
- `plugins/craftflow/scripts/craftflow_stop_verify.py` — ported from
  `xai-grok-hooks`'s stop-verify guard example concept: an opt-in Stop-hook
  gate that blocks session completion until a configured verify command
  passes.
- `plugins/craftflow/scripts/craftflow_hook_trust.py` — ported from
  `xai-grok-hooks`'s `trust.rs` concept: a hash-manifest-based
  provenance/trust gate that fail-closed refuses an unmanifested or
  hash-mismatched repo-local hook script.

No upstream Rust source was copied — all three are original Python
implementations built on this plugin's own existing conventions
(`craftflow_hooklib.py`'s stdin-JSON/hook-decision helpers, and
`craftflow_hook_selfcheck.py`'s subprocess-only/never-import-the-checked-
script isolation pattern). Deliberately NOT ported: grok's HTTP hook runner
(`runner/http.rs`) — deferred, out of this phase's scope.
